Comment (internal/api/handler/oscal/system_security_plans.go:4427):
The handler documents component-uuid as immutable, but updateByComponentMetadata currently only validates that a non-empty component-uuid is a valid UUID; if a client sends a different (valid) component-uuid, it will be silently ignored (since component_uuid isn’t in the Updates map). It’s safer to either reject mismatches with 400 (immutable) or always overwrite the body value with the stored component UUID to avoid surprising clients.
Replies:
**lisa implementation guidance:** Valid — silently ignoring a differing component-uuid is a surprise, and the godoc already promises immutability.

FIX in `updateByComponentMetadata` (internal/api/handler/oscal/system_security_plans.go). The block currently reads:

    oscalBC.UUID = bc.ID.String()
    if strings.TrimSpace(oscalBC.ComponentUuid) == "" {
        oscalBC.ComponentUuid = bc.ComponentUUID.String()
    } else if _, err := uuid.Parse(oscalBC.ComponentUuid); err != nil {
        return ctx.JSON(http.StatusBadRequest, api.NewError(fmt.Errorf("component-uuid must be a valid UUID")))
    }

Change the non-empty branch so that a valid-but-different component-uuid is REJECTED with 400 rather than ignored. Keep the empty case (default to the stored value) — omitting it must stay legal, since UnmarshalOscal MustParses it and a missing value would otherwise panic into a 500.

Reject with the same shape used for the other immutable identities in this PR (see the inherited/satisfied PUTs, which 400 on a provided-uuid / responsibility-uuid change), e.g.:

    if trimmed := strings.TrimSpace(oscalBC.ComponentUuid); trimmed == "" {
        oscalBC.ComponentUuid = bc.ComponentUUID.String()
    } else {
        parsedComponentUUID, err := uuid.Parse(trimmed)
        if err != nil { 400 "component-uuid must be a valid UUID" }
        if parsedComponentUUID != bc.ComponentUUID {
            400 "component-uuid is immutable: it identifies which component this by-component describes, and the offering-item coherence check joins on it"
        }
    }

Both by-component PUTs (requirement- and statement-level) route through this one helper, so one change covers both.

Add a unit test in ssp_shared_responsibility_test.go next to the other immutability tests: PUT with a different valid component-uuid -> 400 and the stored ComponentUUID is unchanged; PUT omitting component-uuid entirely -> 200 (still legal).

